Chocolatey download in windows:

    To install Chocolatey on Windows 10 or 11, the easiest method is to run the installation script directly through PowerShell using standard administrative commands.
However, since you want to utilize GitHub, you can pull the official runtime files from Chocolatey’s GitHub releases, which allows you to install it via an official MSI installer or do a completely offline installation using a local script.
Here are the two ways to install Chocolatey using GitHub resources:

Method 1: The Modern Way (Using the GitHub Release MSI with WinGet)

Chocolatey packages the official engine into an installer hosted directly on the Chocolatey GitHub Repository. You can pull and install it directly via the Windows command line:
1. Right-click the Start menu and select Terminal (Admin) or PowerShell (Admin).
2. Run the following command to download and install the version hosted in the GitHub metadata repository via Windows Package Manager:powershell
winget install --id chocolatey.chocolatey --source winget
Use code with caution.
3. Restart your terminal window to reload the system path.

Method 2: The Manual/Offline Way (Downloading from GitHub Releases)

If you are setting up an air-gapped machine or need to archive the installer:
1. Go to the official Chocolatey GitHub Releases Page.
2. Scroll down to Assets under the latest stable release version and download the chocolatey.<version>.nupkg file. (Note: a .nupkg file is just a zip archive containing the Chocolatey binaries).
3. Right-click the Start Menu, open PowerShell (Admin), and change your execution policy so Windows allows local setup scripts to run:powershell
Set-ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Scope Process -Force
Use code with caution.
4. Extract the .nupkg file using any extraction software (like 7-Zip) and run the internal chocolateyInstall.ps1 script located inside the tools folder.

Method 3: The Standard Remote Script

If you are following popular developer setup scripts shared on GitHub Gists, they typically trigger the official Chocolatey handshake protocol through administrative PowerShell:
powershell
Set-ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Scope Process -Force; [System.Net.ServicePointManager]::SecurityProtocol = [System.Net.ServicePointManager]::SecurityProtocol -bor 3072; iex ((New-Object System.Net.WebClient).DownloadString('https://community.chocolatey.org/install.ps1'))
Use code with caution.

Verifying Your Setup

After using any of the methods above, open a new PowerShell window and run:
powershell
choco --version
Use code with caution.
If it returns a version number (e.g., 2.x.x), Chocolatey is successfully installed and ready to deploy software like Docker or Git!



Using Chocolatey:

    <--------    To download and install Docker Desktop on Windows using Chocolatey, follow these simple steps:

Step 1: Open PowerShell as an Administrator

1. Click the Windows Start menu.
2. Search for PowerShell.
3. Right-click Windows PowerShell and select Run as administrator.

Step 2: Run the Chocolatey Command

Type or copy the following command into your administrative PowerShell window and press Enter:
powershell
choco install docker-desktop -y
Use code with caution.
(Note: The -y flag automatically approves all confirmation prompts during the download and installation process).

Step 3: Complete the Setup

1. Reboot your PC: Chocolatey will download the official installer and configure system dependencies. A system restart is usually required to finalize things.
2. Launch Docker Desktop: Once your computer restarts, search for Docker Desktop in your Start menu and open the application to accept the service agreement.
