Step 3: Run the Setup

1. Double-click the downloaded installer (or right-click and choose Run as administrator).
2. When prompted, ensure "Use WSL 2 instead of Hyper-V" is checked.
3. Follow the on-screen prompts and click Close and restart once the installation succeeds.

Step 4: Verify the Installation

1. Launch Docker Desktop from your Start Menu and accept the Service Agreement.
2. Open PowerShell or Command Prompt and run the following command to ensure the Docker daemon is responding:bash
docker run hello-world
